UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53861575523802
DTSTART:20261115T180000Z
DTEND:20261116T020000Z
DESCRIPTION:Stanford University Libraries presents A Vision of Paris: the R
 oxane Debuisson Collection at Stanford\, on view in the Peterson Gallery a
 nd Munger Rotunda of the Cecil H. Green Library from September 22\, 2026 t
 o January 24\, 2027. \n\nRoxane Debuisson (1927–2018) dedicated sixty ye
 ars to documenting the transformation of the city of Paris during the nine
 teenth century.  If Roxane Debuisson could not stop the changes she saw un
 derway in the late 20th century\, she could at least preserve the city’s
  earlier history through images\, literature\, guidebooks\, and other docu
 ments. \n\nHer lifelong project helped to document Paris during the ninete
 enth century\, especially the city’s rapid changes from the 1850s to the
  1870s\, when Emperor Napoleon III and his prefect of the Seine\, Baron Eu
 gène Haussmann\, transformed the city with new boulevards\, green spaces\
 , and public utilities\, and fostered innovations in commercial and cultur
 al practices. \n\nA Vision of Paris: the Roxane Debuisson Collection at St
 anford draws upon the extensive array of commercial almanacs\, prints\, po
 stcards\, commercial ephemera\, stereographs\, manuscripts\, historic phot
 ographs\, and other items that are a part of the Roxane Debuisson Collecti
 on of Paris history\, circa 1789-1970\, acquired by the Department of Spec
 ial Collections at Stanford University Libraries in 2020. These materials 
 place Paris as the birthplace of political\, commercial\, and urban innova
 tions\, and as a city defined by the tension between its historical past a
 nd its continuous reinvention. The exhibit highlights the city’s rapid c
 hanges and their diverse causes\, while suggesting the collection’s vast
  possibilities for both research and instruction.\n\nThis exhibition is cu
 rated by Sarah Sussman\, Assistant University Librarian for Collections an
 d Services & Curator of French and Italian Collections\, Stanford Universi
 ty Libraries\, and Chloe Summers Edmondson\, Assistant Professor of French
  at the University of Miami. Produced and designed by Deardra Fuzzell\, wi
 th assistance from Kylee Jo Diedrich\, Sofia McGullam Ornelas\, and Pasha 
 Tope.\n\nA Vision of Paris: the Roxane Debuisson Collection at Stanford wi
 ll be open to the public. Registration at the entrance with a valid govern
 ment ID is required to enter the Cecil H. Green Library and view the exhib
 it.
GEO:37.426984;-122.167998
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
SUMMARY:A Vision of Paris: The Roxane Debuisson Collection at Stanford
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.stanford.edu/event/a-vision-of-paris-the-roxan
 e-debuisson-collection-at-stanford
CATEGORIES:Exhibition
END:VEVENT
